nizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-22T22:20:09Z","updated_at":"2021-03-22T22:20:09Z","body":"Typeorm overwrites my enums with the Postgres driver as well.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/804433729/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sannajammeh","id":50969683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwOTY5Njgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50969683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh","html_url":"https://github.com/sannajammeh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sannajammeh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/826047178","html_url":"https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/4897#issuecomment-826047178","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/4897","id":826047178,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgyNjA0NzE3OA==","user":{"login":"Dezzmeister","id":29151915,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTUxOTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29151915?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/Dezzmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-24T07:04:04Z","updated_at":"2021-04-24T07:20:10Z","body":"I am having the same issue with Postgres 13. As far as I have tested, this issue is present in typeorm v0.2.32 and has been present since 0.2.21. To reproduce:\r\n1. Create an entity with an enum member. Do not give the enum member a default value, and make it non nullable.\r\n2. Create (do not generate) a migration. In the migration, create a table for the entity and populate it with rows for which the value of the enum is not identical.\r\n3. Run the migration and start the server.\r\n4. The server should crash when typeorm tries to destroy your table. This is because it tries to set an entire column to null, but since null values are not allowed and there is no default, the server crashes and you get a handy stacktrace.\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: I found a hacky fix. If you append \"_enum\" to the name of your enum (in the database), typeorm won't take a wrecking ball to your data. I'm not sure, but I think typeorm is converting the camel-case name of your enum in the code to a snake-case name and appending \"_enum,\" then creating a new type with this name (identical to the existing enum) and trying to set this as the type of the column in your table. \r\n\r\n\r\nFor example; I had an \"image\" table with an \"image_category\" enum. In the code, this enum was called \"ImageCategory.\" I found that typeorm crashed when trying to run the query `ALTER TABLE \"image\" ADD \"category\" \"image_category_enum\" NOT NULL`. It had created a type named by converting \"ImageCategory\" to snake case and appending \"_enum.\" I was able to fix this issue by reverting the migration and renaming the enum (in the db) to \"image_category_enum.\"","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/826047178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Dezzmeister","id":29151915,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTUxOTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29151915?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/Dezzmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dezzmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}}]